# ============================================================================
# timing.sdc - SafeVision B chain bring-up tops
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Covers BOTH bring-up tops (whatever TOP_MODULE the TD project points at):
#     top_stage5_sector_rd / top_stage6_fat32_mount - single 50 MHz domain, no PLL
#     top_sdram_loopback                            - 50 MHz refclk -> sys_pll,
#                                                     logic runs on C1 = 125 MHz
#
#   clk = pin R7 = net FPGA_GCLK = board 50 MHz oscillator -> period 20 ns.
#
# ★ derive_clocks is required once a PLL is instantiated (top_sdram_loopback).
#   Without it the 125 MHz PLL outputs have no clock definition, the SDRAM
#   application logic is never timed, and STA reports a FALSE pass.
#   For the PLL-free tops it derives nothing extra, so it is safe to keep.
#
# Deliberately NOT constrained yet, and why:
#   sd_dclk (SPI SCLK) : generated by a divider from clk; 200 kHz during card
#                        init and 12.5 MHz for data.  It is a slow, unsynchronized
#                        output and no I/O delay numbers exist until measured
#                        (checklist M-5).  Add output delay later if STA asks.
#   sd_mosi / sd_ncs   : same reasoning, no measured I/O delays yet.
#   uart_txd           : 115200 baud, about 87 us per bit; not timing critical.
#   rst_n (KEY_1)      : asynchronous button feeding the first stage of
#                        reset_sync.  Enable the optional false path below only
#                        after bring-up if STA reports violations on that path.
#
# The product design (sys_clk / mem_clk / pixel_clk / serial_clk / audio_clk
# from TD PLL IP, per docs/interface_spec.md section 1) will add derive_clocks
# and set_clock_groups of its own.  This file belongs to the bring-up top only.
# ============================================================================

create_clock -name clk -period 20 -waveform {0 10} [get_ports {clk}]

# Auto-derive the PLL output clocks (sys_pll C0/C1/C2 ...) from the master clock.
derive_clocks

# Optional, enable after bring-up if the async button path is reported:
# set_false_path -from [get_ports {rst_n}]